[Applause]  [Music]  February is behind us which means this  episode of new releases is taking a  top-down look at the month of March the  new month brings us a bunch of entries  in some beloved series for everyone from  action junkies to sports fans in fact  there's so much that this episode  includes a bonus sixth recommendation so  let's jump right into some of the  hottest games coming in March the month  kicks off with pokemon mystery dungeon  rescue team DX you may recall red and  blue rescue teams on the original DS and  this new deluxe version includes all the  content from both dressed in a new  spiffy-looking watercolor inspired art  style you'll fight and turn-based  battles as you explore the game's many  dungeons but rather than catch new  monsters and pokeballs  you'll be recruiting them onto your  rescue team this re-release even  includes mega evolutions it's coming  exclusively to switch on Friday March  6th but you can download a demo from the  eShop right now you can also go  exploring in Ori and the will of the  wisps which makes some pretty  significant changes from the first game  this sequel trades the manual checkpoint  system for auto-saves  and instead of purchasing sequential  upgrades you'll collect shards to spend  on various abilities and items but you  can still expect the same level of  Metroidvania exploration in combat as  you go beyond the forest of the first  game the adventure begins on Xbox one  and PC on Wednesday the 11th and yes it  will be available on game paths  March has another sequel that's changing  things up with neo 2 this game is  actually set before the events of neo so  you'll be creating a custom character  instead of controlling William Adams  you'll still have to switch stances and  maintain your stamina and health as you  battle big bosses but this time around  you can take them on and three player  co-op what's more you can actually  transform into a youkai yourself if you  acquire a monster's soul core neo 2 is a  ps4 exclusive launching Friday the 13th  here's hoping we get a new Twitter  stance as DLC after that  let's trade our samurai swords for  baseball bats with another ps4 exclusive  MLB the show 20 last year's game  included the minor leagues but not any  of the actual players this time the  minor league players likenesses are  actually included team and logo editing  is also moving to franchise mode before  this you could only use it in diamond  dynasty you can see the changes for  yourself on Tuesday the 17th I don't  know if Animal Crossing New Horizons has  baseball but it does have plenty of  other outdoor activities for you to  enjoy the latest entry in the cutesy  series is set on an island one that you  can actually terraform to your liking  using the new Nook phone there's almost  too much new stuff to even list here  from new animal friends to seasonal  updates to finally being able to  customize your villager from the start  it's all happening only on switch on  Friday the 20th that same day we're  getting a game on the total opposite end  of the spectrum doom eternal there's a  lot of new stuff to talk about in this  sequel to like the doom Slayers  grappling hook and flamethrower which  add even more chaos to the game's  frenetic combat there's also an  asymmetrical multiplayer mode where one  Slayer takes on two player controlled  demons speaking of which there are  plenty of new demons to take on in the  campaign - including the tomb hunter and  Marauder doom eternal hits ps4 xbox one  pc and stadia on the 20th with a switch  version planned for later this year and  those are some of the hottest games  launching all month long as always  remember that release dates are based on  retailer listings and are subject to  change thanks for watching guys and I'll  be back with a deeper look at more March  games next Sunday

